  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing the Global Health Security Agenda through Strengthening Capacities for Rapid Response to Humanitarian and Public Health Emergencies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this collaboration with the US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), IOM will capitalize and build on its health technical and operational expertise to better respond to humanitarian and public health emergencies globally. IOM will strengthen its capacity to rapidlyrespond to humanitarian and public health emergencies through the recruitment of personnel dedicated to improving staff capacity for rapidresponse and assess of IOM&apos;s existing health information systems and conducting capacity building trainings. This initiative will complement IOM&apos;s contribution to the Global Health Security Agenda (GHSA), including the implementation of the CDC-RFA-GH15-1632 cooperative agreement on global health security partnership engagement. IOM also intends to work with implementing partners from within CDC-RFA-GH16-1719cooperative agreement, with potential collaborators including Johns Hopkins University and The Eastern Mediterranean Public Health Network (EMPHNET) on emergency training modules and field level epidemiological investigations.</narrative>
  </description>
